{
"classname" "game_messagebox"
"origin" "-808 -616 616"
"targetname" "info_weather"
"title" "Weather"
"message" "rain is a func_rainvolume (Start Active) over the west half: Raindrops per update 300, Wind X 100, Wind Y 200, so every drop slants the same way. Rain and snow only fall where the sky is above.\n\nSTORM fires two trigger_changevalues that set the rain's Raindrops per update to 900 and Wind X to 400; CALM sets them back to 300 and 100. Every player sees the change at once.\n\nThe east half is a func_snowvolume with Snowflakes per update 300.\n\nThe box at the north wall is an env_fogzone: Density 0.004, Fog color 150 150 160. From outside it looks like haze; inside, the fog thickens the deeper you go."
}
